-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-

  If installing for the FIRST time, skip to the next -=-=-=-=- line...

  Those SysOps using v1.00 thru v1.03 of Rush Hour, follow these steps to
update your versions to this NEW version:

1. It will be necessary for you to DELETE the "RushHour.data" file located
   inside your "doors:RushHour/" directory.

2. Now REPLACE the Main, History, and ReadMe files in your RushHour/ directory
   with those contained in this NEW archive.

3. The first person to enter the game will create the NEW "RushHour.data" file,
   which stores ADDITIONAL information about how each player played the game.
   For info as to why it didn't CONVERT your existing file, see the HISTORY
   file for specifics!

-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-

  To install this game onto your CNet Amiga, v3.05c or v4.53, follow these
easy steps:

1. Create a directory in your DOORS or PFILES section called "RushHour/".

2. Copy the "RushHour.Main" file, as well as this README and the HISTORY file
   into the directory you created above.

3. Add the "RushHour.Main" file as a CNet ARexx pfile/door.

  Once installed, the first person to load the game will create additional
files inside the "RushHour/" directory. These include High Score files, in
addition to a data file used to store which Level and Card each player on
your BBS left off at(as well as other info) when they exit the program.

